  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The Elemental Analysis of Glass Beads (2022), published by Leuven University Press, has been cited 12 times — enough that OpenAlex puts it in the top 10% of works in its field and year. Beyond that, it has been downloaded 3,567 times.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The Elemental Analysis of Glass Beads by Laure Dussubieux and Heather Walder was published by Leuven University Press in 2022. Conceptually, the work connects to Bead, TRACE (psycholinguistics), Materials science, Archaeology and History.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">OpenAlex records 12 citations. That places it in the top 10% of works in its field and year of publication. Citations peaked in 2023 with 3 citing works. Notable citing venues include Archaeometry, ACS symposium series and Heritage Science. The citing works include 7 journal articles, 1 book chapter and 1 preprint. They come from 9 countries, led by the United States, the United Kingdom and Poland.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">It has been downloaded 3,567 times via OAPEN. Its subject matter aligns with Life below water among the Sustainable Development Goals. The work was funded by KU Leuven.</p>",
  "events": {},
